{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1082", "sample_idx": 28, "model_name": "qwen/qwen3.5-397b-a17b", "content": "Arthur woke to the familiar chirp of his alarm, but something felt unnervingly rigid about the morning light filtering through his blinds. As he reached for his coffee mug, his hand clipped slightly through the handle before snapping back into place with a subtle, digital jitter that sent a chill down his spine. He looked out the window and noticed the neighbors walking in perfect, looping patterns, their faces devoid of micro-expressions, while a faint, translucent bar hovered in the corner of his vision displaying a health meter that decreased every time he stubbed his toe on the bedframe. The realization didn't hit him all at once but rather assembled itself like a loading screen, piece by piece, until the terrifying truth settled in: the texture of his own skin looked slightly pixelated under close inspection, and the world around him rendered only when he directly focused on it.\n\n***\n\nPanic surged through him as he tried to scream, but no sound came out, only a generic error icon flashing above his head. He ran to the front door, expecting to escape into the street, but found himself blocked by an invisible wall that shimmered with a grid-like pattern whenever he pressed against it. A system message popped up in mid-air, cold and impersonal, stating that the current quest line had not yet been unlocked for this character. Arthur slumped against the barrier, watching as a floating cursor appeared in his peripheral vision, hovering waitingly over his shoulder as if controlled by an unseen player deciding his next move. He was no longer the protagonist of his own life but merely an avatar waiting for input, trapped in a loop of code he could never hope to rewrite.", "logprobs": [{"token": "Arthur", "logprob": -0.00039090405}, {"token": " woke", "logprob": -0.0016316964}, {"token": " to", "logprob": -0.00035542605}, {"token": " the", "logprob": 0.0},